// expected: undefined: fmt.Stringer
//
// A qualified type is only legal when its package is in scope: the file imports
// it, or the signature being resolved belongs to a package whose imports we are
// carrying for a monomorphization.
//
// Legacy rejects this source with `undefined: fmt`, stage4 with the member form.
// Until round 84 it ALSO crashed the compiler on roughly 2-7% of runs instead:
// the unresolved variadic element type left the parameter's type nil, and
// wrapVariadicArgs then built the variadic slice with that nil type, so the
// element size and the slice header came from garbage and the compiler died in
// runtime.memcpy with a stack address as a length. The builder now refuses to
// synthesize a value of a type it could not resolve.
//
// The BARE form (`...Undefined`) is pinned separately by
// reject_undefined_variadic_type; both are the same rule reached by different
// paths.
package main

func f(args ...fmt.Stringer) {}

func main() {
	var s fmt.Stringer = int32(1)
	f(s)
}
